<title>SWEDEN: Electrolux 1996 sales down five pct.</title>
<headline>Electrolux 1996 sales down five pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		3,250   vs     4,016</p>
<p> Turnover				110,000   vs   115,800</p>
<p> Operating costs		     101,150   vs   106,082</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	  12.50   vs     12.50</p>
<p> Operating profit			4,450   vs     5,311</p>
<p> Depreciation			    4,400   vs     4,407</p>
<p> Net financial items	  CHARGE 1,200   vs     1,295 CHARGE</p>
<p> Minorities		     CHARGE   250   vs	  69 CHARGE</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			  3,000   vs     3,947</p>
<p> Tax					 1,150   vs     1,199</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)			    25.30   vs     37.50</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts polled by Reuters expected a profit after financial items for 1996 of 3.49 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1003</p>
